meta {
  name: Propose product edit (VERIFIED)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/edits
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Better Product Name",
    "salt": 1.5
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setEnvVar("editId", res.getBody().editId);
  }
}

docs {
  TICKET-P5-006 (re-keyed in TICKET-P6-009) — Propose a change to a VERIFIED product. Registered
  users only. `:productId` must be a UUID (400 { code: 'invalid_product_id' } otherwise).

  Send ONLY the changed fields (partial payload). Editable fields span both tables but stay flat in
  the request: name, brand (Product), genericName, energyKcal, fat, saturatedFat, carbohydrates,
  sugars, protein, salt, servingSize, ingredients (PackagedProduct), productImageKey (Product.image,
  when the photo was replaced). Unknown fields are rejected. Values equal to the current product value
  are dropped server-side; an effectively empty diff is a 422 (no_changes).

  The edit is stored as PENDING with an originalValues snapshot; two other registered users must
  approve before it is applied. The DB enforces one PENDING edit per product via a partial unique
  index (one_pending_edit_per_product, now keyed on productId).

  On 201 the post-response script stores `editId` for the vote/dismiss requests.

  Errors:
  - 401 — unauthenticated
  - 403 — anonymous user
  - 404 — product not found, including REJECTED ({ error: 'product_not_found' })
  - 409 — pending edit already exists ({ error: 'edit_pending' }) or product not VERIFIED ({ error: 'product_not_verified' })
  - 422 — validation failure / no changes
}
